# E21 -- Three cavern layers rotated with the surface on CTRL for a season. Land and cavern layers managed: every in-embark entry allowed and assigned by the matrix, groups on (one scheduler over every layer, as v5.7 ships it), coupling and ecology off. 100,800 ticks, two replicates. Every 3,000 ticks the wild units are counted per layer and the groups status printed. Questions: do cavern arrivals follow their assigned seasons; does a gated or resident cavern group stop surface waves (the scheduler's max_concurrent counts every layer today).
